  "name": "Question 8",
  "problem": "David needs to decide what bag of flour to buy from three different types available at the grocery store:\n\n- Bag $A$ weighs $5$ kilograms, and costs $$7.50\\,.$\n\n- Bag $B$ weighs $2$ kilograms, and costs $$3.20\\,.$\n\n- Bag $C$ weighs $1$ kilogram, and costs $$1.70\\,.$\n\nWhich bag of flour is the best deal?",
  "worked_solution": "The best deal is the one with the lowest unit price. So, we need to compute the unit prices for all three bags. To compute the unit price, we divide the cost by the total number of kilograms.\n\n- Dividing the total cost by the number of kilograms in bag $A$, we get\n\n$$\n7.50÷5=1.50\\,.\n$$\n\nSo, the unit price of bag $A$ is $$1.50$ per kilogram.\n\n- Dividing the total cost by the number of kilograms in bag $B$, we get\n\n$$\n3.20÷2=1.60\\,.\n$$\n\nSo, the unit price of bag $B$ is $$1.60$ per kilogram.\n\n- Dividing the total cost by the number of kilograms in bag $C$, we get\n\n$$\n1.70÷1=1.70\\,.\n$$\n\nSo, the unit price of bag $C$ is $$1.70$ per kilogram.\n\nFrom the above, we see that bag $A$ has the lowest unit price. Therefore, bag $A$ is the best deal.",
